[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "Queen's Gambit Declined"]
[Variation "Queen's Gambit Declined: Three Knights Variation"]
[ECO "D37"]
[Character "solid,positional"]
[Risk "low"]
[EarlyMate "none"]
[Tricks "none"]
[Themes "qgd-setup,transposition,castle-early"]
[For "black"]
[Kind "sideline"]
[Opponent "4.Nf3"]
[Start "orthodox 3...Nf6"]

4. Nf3 { Develops the king's knight first and keeps the choice for the c1 bishop: g5, f4, or stay at home behind e3. } 4... Be7 5. Bg5 ( 5. Bf4 { The same position as 4.Bf4 Be7 5.Nf3: Black castles and hits d4 with ...c5. } 5... O-O 6. e3 c5 ) ( 5. e3 { The 4.e3 line by another move order: Black castles, waits for Bd3, then plays ...dxc4 and ...c5. } 5... O-O ) ( 5. cxd5 { The Exchange Variation by another move order: Black recaptures with the e-pawn, then ...c6 and ...Bf5. } 5... exd5 6. Bg5 c6 7. e3 Bf5 ) ( 5. Qc2 O-O 6. e3 ) 5... O-O { Castles before the centre opens. The bishop on e7 already breaks the pin on f6. } 6. e3 Nbd7 *
